srow(131, 3, 'MATERIAL', '"PINCHAS SON OF ELEAZAR SON OF AARON THE PRIEST" — THE LINEAGE TRACED AGAINST SIMEON\'S TAUNT: PRIEST SON OF PRIEST, ZEALOT SON OF ZEALOT, TURNER-AWAY SON OF TURNER-AWAY. The tribe of Simeon against Levi: "would the son of the daughter of THIS FATTENER (Jethro, who fattened calves for idolatry — Exod 6:25\'s "one of the daughters of PUTIEL", read as Jethro\'s line; computed) uproot a whole tribe?" — so the LORD traces his lineage (25:11): a priest son of a priest; a ZEALOT son of a zealot (Levi at Shechem, Gen 34:25); a TURNER-AWAY of wrath son of a turner-away of wrath (Aaron, 17:13 — "he stood between the dead and the living, and the plague was stayed") — THE SIFREI\'S THREE-GENERATION TITLE READ AS THREE DEEDS, and the ink carries the pairing itself: "and the plague was stayed" at 17:13 and 25:8, "and he atoned for" at 17:12 and 25:13 — the father\'s censer and the son\'s spear in one clause and one verb (computed on the tokens: the two seats of each). The exam: Sanhedrin 82b (the taunt and the lineage); Sotah 43a, Bava Batra 109b-110a (Putiel — Jethro who fattened calves, or Joseph who mastered his passion); Zevachim 101b (Phinehas made a priest by the deed — the priesthood "given" here).')
srow(131, 4, 'MATERIAL', '"BEHOLD, I GIVE HIM MY COVENANT OF PEACE" — TWELVE HIGH PRIESTS IN THE FIRST TEMPLE, EIGHTY IN THE SECOND WITH SHORTENED LIVES FOR SELLING THE OFFICE; "THE FOAL HAS OUTWEIGHED THE MENORAH". "Therefore say: behold, I give him My covenant of peace" (25:12) — from him descended TWELVE high priests in the first Temple; in the second Temple EIGHTY, whose lives shortened "because they sold the high-priesthood for money" — one sent two silver urns rimmed with silver, another two gold rimmed with gold: "the FOAL has outweighed the MENORAH" (the counts a data row of the shelf; Yoma 9a\'s "more than three hundred" the Talmud\'s own figure against the Sifrei\'s eighty — a DISPUTE inside the shelf on the number; the ink: "My covenant of peace" one seat, Malachi\'s covenant with Levi "life and peace", computed). The exam: Yoma 9a (the second Temple\'s high priests and their years), 18a (the sale of the office); Sifrei\'s eighty against Yoma\'s three hundred — a dispute row.')
srow(131, 5, 'MATERIAL', '"A COVENANT OF ETERNAL PRIESTHOOD" — THE TWENTY-FOUR PRIESTLY GIFTS; "BECAUSE HE WAS ZEALOUS" — READY TO GIVE HIS LIFE; "AND HE WILL ATONE" — NOT "TO ATONE": HE STANDS AND ATONES UNTIL THE RESURRECTION. "And it shall be to him and to his seed after him a covenant of eternal priesthood" (25:13): THE TWENTY-FOUR PRIESTLY GIFTS bestowed on the priests (chapter 18\'s dues counted by the shelf as twenty-four — the data channel\'s number, Bava Kamma 110b\'s list; the ink: "everlasting priesthood" at Exod 40:15 and here alone, the sons\' anointing narrowed to Phinehas\'s line, computed); "because he was zealous for his God" — because he was ready to GIVE HIS LIFE; "and he will atone for the children of Israel" — IT IS NOT WRITTEN "TO ATONE" (the infinitive) BUT "AND HE WILL ATONE" (the vav-form): until now he has not stirred, but he STANDS AND ATONES UNTIL THE REVIVAL OF THE DEAD — the Sifrei reads the vav-prefixed form as a FUTURE where the morphology tags it NARRATIVE PAST ("and he atoned", the intensive stem\'s "and he did" form) and Onkelos renders a past ("and he atoned"): the shelf\'s reading of the form recorded against the tag and the translation — a dispute on the tense of one word, the ink\'s form the evidence (computed on the tag). The exam: Bava Kamma 110b (the twenty-four gifts); Zevachim 101b; Sanhedrin 82b; the tense-reading against the parser\'s morphology tag.')
